DEFINITION OF DONE

The audit is complete only when:

- The actual architecture has been traced.
- All three plans have been checked.
- Payment verification and webhook security have been reviewed.
- Exact entitlement rules have been tested.
- Cancellation, renewal, and expiration behavior have been reviewed.
- The renewal panel has been tested.
- Important failure and security cases have been covered.
- Relevant automated tests have been executed where possible.
- Confirmed defects have been fixed safely or clearly documented.
- Remaining blockers are explicit.
- The final readiness verdict reflects the evidence, not assumptions.

Begin by inspecting the repository and mapping the existing implementation. Do not start by rewriting code. Perform the audit in phases, preserve working functionality, and report concrete evidence throughout.